{"id":45,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 2947 lines, 172452 bytes --\n2760 | integrand into `|Fourier coefficients|²`.  See `docs/gap_analysis.md` for the\n2761 | full analysis.\n2762 | -/\n2763 | \n2764 | /-- **Clean factorization of the reflection-positivity integrand.**\n2765 | \n2766 | `osG(U) · osG(θU) = f(U) · f(θU) · exp(-β S_W(U))`.\n2767 | \n2768 | This is a purely algebraic identity: it follows from the reflection symmetries\n2769 | `S⁺(θU) = S⁻(U)` and `S_int(θU) = S_int(U)`, together with the action\n2770 | decomposition `S_W = S⁺ + S⁻ + S_int`.  No support hypothesis on `f` is needed. -/\n2771 | lemma osG_thetaG_factorization\n2772 |     (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T)\n2773 |     (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ)\n2774 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) :\n2775 |     osG N T L β f U * osG N T L β f (reflectLinkVariable N U) =\n2776 |     f U * f (reflectLinkVariable N U) *\n2777 |     Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFinite N β (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) U) := by\n2778 |   unfold osG\n2779 |   have h_pos_reflect : wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β (reflectLinkVariable N U) =\n2780 |       wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β U :=\n2781 |     (neg_action_reflection_os_periodic N T L β hT U).symm\n2782 |   have h_int_reflect : wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β (reflectLinkVariable N U) =\n2783 |       wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U :=\n2784 |     interface_action_reflection_symmetric_os_periodic N T L β hT U\n2785 |   have h_total : wilsonActionFinite N β (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) U =\n2786 |       wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U + wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β U +\n2787 |       wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U :=\n2788 |     total_decomposition_os_periodic N T L β U\n2789 |   rw [h_pos_reflect, h_int_reflect, h_total]\n2790 |   -- Split the RHS exp(-β*(S⁺+S⁻+S_int)) into a product of four exp's matching the LHS\n2791 |   rw [show (-β * (wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U + wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β U +\n2792 |       wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U) : ℝ) =\n2793 |       (-β * wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U) + (-β * wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β U) +\n2794 |       (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U) by ring]\n2795 |   rw [Real.exp_add, Real.exp_add]\n2796 |   rw [show (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U : ℝ) =\n2797 |       (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U / 2) + (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U / 2)\n2798 |       by ring]\n2799 |   rw [Real.exp_add]\n2800 |   ring\n2801 | \n2802 | /-- **Step 2: Pointwise character expansion of the reflection-positivity integrand.**\n2803 | \n2804 | Substituting the character expansion of `exp(-β·S_int)` (from\n2805 | `interface_boltzmann_character_expansion`) into the factorization\n2806 | `osG(U)·osG(θU) = f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β·S_pos)·exp(-β·S_neg)·exp(-β·S_int)`\n2807 | (from `osG_thetaG_factorization` + `total_decomposition_os_periodic`), the\n2808 | integrand admits the pointwise expansion (viewed in ℂ)\n2809 | \n2810 |     (osG(U)·osG(θU) : ℂ) = (C : ℂ) · ∑_w (F w : ℂ) · ↑r(U) · Φ_w(U) · Ψ_w(U) · V_w(U)\n2811 | \n2812 | with `C > 0`, `F(w) ≥ 0`, and `r(U) = f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β·S_pos(U))·exp(-β·S_neg(U))`\n2813 | (the real prefactor from the positive and negative bulk actions).  The\n2814 | character factors `Φ_w`, `Ψ_w`, `V_w` are the same as in\n2815 | `interface_boltzmann_character_expansion`.  This is step 2 of the formalization\n2816 | path in §8.11.53.  Pure algebra — 0 sorries, uses `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette`\n2817 | (axiom count 6, unchanged). -/\n2818 | lemma osG_thetaG_eq_char_expansion_pointwise\n2819 |     (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) (hN : 1 ≤ N)\n2820 |     (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) :\n2821 |     ∃ (C : ℝ) (hC : 0 < C)\n2822 |       (ι : Type) (hι : Fintype ι) (dims : ι → ℕ)\n2823 |       (ρ : ∀ i, SU N →* Matrix (Fin (dims i)) (Fin (d