st the change of variables. The `interface_action_reflection_symmetric_os_periodic` might be needed for a different reason — to show that the kernel `K(U⁺, W⁺) = exp(-β S_int(U⁺, u⁰, θW⁺))` is PD.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The PD of the interface kernel is the key. The kernel is `K(U⁺, W⁺) = exp(-β S_int(U⁺, u⁰, θW⁺))`. This is a function of two positive-half configs `U⁺` and `W⁺` (and the fixed interface `u⁰`). The PD says:\n```\n∫∫ H(U⁺) · conj(H(W⁺)) · K(U⁺, W⁺) dμ⁺(U⁺) dμ⁺(W⁺) ≥ 0\n```\n\nThis PD comes from `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` and `interface_kernel_character_expansion`.\n\nOK so let me now think about the formalization plan. This is quite complex. Let me think about what intermediate lemmas I need.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about the big picture. The formalization has several major pieces:\n\n1. **Transform the integral** from `∫ osG(U)·osG(θU) dμ₀` to `∫∫∫ f(U⁺,u⁰_s)·f(W⁺,u⁰_s)·exp(-βS_pos(U⁺))·exp(-βS_pos(W⁺))·exp(-βS_int(U⁺,u⁰,θW⁺)) dμ⁺ dμ⁰ dμ⁺` using:\n   - `measure_factorization'` (split the measure)\n   - `osG_thetaG_factorization` (factor the integrand)\n   - `total_decomposition_os_periodic` (decompose the action)\n   - `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving_between` (change of variables)\n   - `neg_action_reflection_os_periodic` (transform S_neg → S_pos)\n   - `dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface` (f(θU) = f(W⁺, u⁰_s))\n\n2. **Apply PD of interface kernel** to show the inner double integral (over U⁺ and W⁺) is ≥ 0 for each u⁰.\n\n3. **Integrate over u⁰** to get the full integral ≥ 0.\n\nThis is a LOT of work. Let me think about what's the most tractable first step.\n\nActually, I realize I should look at the PD of the interface kernel more carefully. Let me read `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` and `interface_kernel_character_expansion`.\n\nLet me also check: is there already a lemma that states the PD of the interface kernel in the form I need?\n\nLet me read the PeterWeyl.lean lemmas.","turn":36,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":49,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PeterWeyl.lean\n-- 3735 lines, 209363 bytes --\n350 |   have hSTUV := PositiveDefinite.prod hSTU hV\n351 |   convert hSTUV using 3\n352 | \n353 | /-- **The plaquette Boltzmann factor is positive-definite on `SU(N)⁴`.**\n354 | \n355 | For `c ≥ 0`, the function\n356 |     (g₁, g₂, g₃, g₄) ↦ exp(c · Re Tr(g₁ g₂ g₃ g₄))\n357 | is positive-definite on `SU(N) × SU(N) × SU(N) × SU(N)` (left-associated).\n358 | \n359 | This is the key positive-definiteness input for the Osterwalder-Seiler transfer\n360 | matrix positivity proof.  It is proved from the Peter-Weyl / Clebsch-Gordan\n361 | character expansion axiom `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette`: the expansion\n362 | writes the Boltzmann factor as a finite sum, with non-negative coefficients, of\n363 | products `χ_s(g₁) χ_t(g₂) χ_u(g₃) χ_v(g₄)` of characters, each product\n364 | positive-definite by `charProduct4_positiveDefinite`.  A finite sum of\n365 | positive-definite functions with non-negative coefficients is positive-definite\n366 | (`PositiveDefinite.sum`). -/\n367 | theorem plaquetteBoltzmannPD (N : ℕ) (c : ℝ) (hc : 0 ≤ c) :\n368 |     PositiveDefinite\n369 |       (λ (p : ((SU N × SU N) × SU N) × SU N) =>\n370 |         (Real.exp (c * (Matrix.trace ((p.1.1.1 * p.1.1.2 * p.1.2 * p.2 : SU N) :\n371 |             Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ)).re) : ℂ)) := by\n372 |   obtain ⟨ι, hι, dims, ρ, hU, hMeas, hIrr, hDims, coeff, hcoeff, cg, hcg, hcg_decomp, dual, hdual,\n373 |       cgME, hcgME_decomp, hcgME_unitary,\n374 |       Λ, hΛ, dimsΛ, ρΛ, hUΛ, hIrrΛ, hDimsΛ, emb, hemb, μ, hμ,\n375 |       cgMEΛ, hcgMEΛ_support, hexp4, hL2, hSchurΛ, hcgMEΛ_parts⟩ :=\n376 |     peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette N c hc\n377 |   obtain ⟨hSchurΛ_int, hSchurΛ_diag, hSchurΛ_offdiag⟩ := hSchurΛ\n378 |   obtain ⟨hcgMEΛ_decomp, hcgMEΛ_unitary, hcgMEΛ_support_zero⟩ := hcgMEΛ_parts\n379 |   letI : Fintype ι := hι\n380 |   -- The four-character product, as a function of the plaquette links.\n381 |   let F (r s t u v : ι) (p : ((SU N × SU N) × SU N) × SU N) : ℂ :=\n382 |     repCharacter (ρ s) p.1.1.1 * repCharacter (ρ t) p.1.1.2 *\n383 |     repCharacter (ρ u) p.1.2 * repCharacter (ρ v) p.2\n384 |   have hF_PD : ∀ r s t u v, PositiveDefinite (F r s t u v) :=\n385 |     fun r s t u v => charProduct4_positiveDefinite ρ hU s t u v\n386 |   -- Innermost sum (over v): weighted by the expansion coefficient.\n387 |   have hSv : ∀ r s t u, PositiveDefinite\n388 |       (λ p => ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p) :=\n389 |     fun r s t u =>\n390 |       PositiveDefinite.sum Finset.univ (F r s t u)\n391 |         (fun v _ => hF_PD r s t u v) (coeff r s t u)\n392 |         (fun v _ => hcoeff r s t u v)\n393 |   -- Outer sums (over u, t, s, r): unweighted sums of PD functions.\n394 |   have hSu : ∀ r s t, PositiveDefinite\n395 |       (λ p => ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p) :=\n396 |     fun r s t =>\n397 |       PositiveDefinite.sum' Finset.univ\n398 |         (fun u p => ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p)\n399 |         (fun u _ => hSv r s t u)\n400 |   have hSt : ∀ r s, PositiveDefinite\n401 |       (λ p => ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p) :=\n402 |     fun r s =>\n403 |       PositiveDefinite.sum' Finset.univ\n404 |         (fun t p => ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p)\n405 |         (fun t _ => hSu r s t)\n406 |   have hSs : ∀ r, PositiveDefinite\n407 |       (λ p => ∑ s : ι, ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p) :=\n408 |     fun r =>\n409 |       PositiveDefinite.sum' Finset.univ\n410 |         (fun s p => ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι, (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p)\n411 |         (fun s _ => hSt r s)\n412 |   have hSr : PositiveDefinite\n413 |       (λ p => ∑ r : ι, ∑ s : ι, ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι,\n414 |         (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p) :=\n415 |     PositiveDefinite.sum' Finset.univ\n416 |       (fun r p => ∑ s : ι, ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι,\n417 |         (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p)\n418 |       (fun r _ => hSs r)\n419 |   -- The Boltzmann factor equals the character expansion pointwise.\n420 |   have hfun :\n421 |       (λ p : ((SU N × SU N) × SU N) × SU N =>\n422 |         (Real.exp (c * (Matrix.trace ((p.1.1.1 * p.1.1.2 * p.1.2 * p.2 : SU N) :\n423 |             Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ)).re) : ℂ)) =\n424 |       (λ p => ∑ r : ι, ∑ s : ι, ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι,\n425 |         (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) * F r s t u v p) := by\n426 |     funext p\n427 |     simp only [F]\n428 |     exact hexp4 p.1.1.1 p.1.1.2 p.1.2 p.2\n429 |   rw [hfun]\n430 |   exact hSr\n431 | \n432 | /-- A product of four characters with the 3rd and 4th conjugated,\n433 | `χ_s(g₁) · χ_t(g₂) · conj(χ_u(g₃)) · conj(χ_v(g₄))`, is positive-definite on\n434 | `SU(N)⁴` (left-associated).  This follows from `charProduct4_positiveDefinite`\n435 | and `PositiveDefinite.conj` applied to the 3rd and 4th factors. -/\n436 | lemma charProduct4_inv_positiveDefinite {ι : Type*} {dims : ι → ℕ}\n437 |     (ρ : ∀ i, SU N →* Matrix (Fin (dims i)) (Fin (dims i)) ℂ)\n438 |     (hU : ∀ i, IsUnitaryRepresentation (ρ i))\n439 |     (s t u v : ι) :\n\n... 3296 more line(s) below (use offset=440 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-10 01:05:14 UTC","timestamp":1786323914,"token_count":1627,"tool_call_id":"2db3a030-1f76-4fb8-acf5-ec906f6b1687","full_token_estimate":1238,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PeterWeyl.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":3735,"byte_count":209363,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":36,"is_prune_marker":false}
