{"id":52,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PeterWeyl.lean\n-- 3735 lines, 209363 bytes --\n1600 |       ∏ l ∈ L_V, repCharacter (ρ (w l)) (g l) := by\n1601 |     rw [map_prod]\n1602 |     exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun l hl => by rw [hdual, Complex.conj_conj]\n1603 |   -- `univ` is the disjoint union of `univ \\ L_V` and `L_V`.\n1604 |   have h_disj : Disjoint ((Finset.univ : Finset L) \\ L_V) L_V :=\n1605 |     Finset.disjoint_left.mpr fun _ ha => (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).2\n1606 |   have h_eq : ((Finset.univ : Finset L) \\ L_V) ∪ L_V = Finset.univ := by\n1607 |     ext x; simp\n1608 |   rw [h_conj, ← Finset.prod_union h_disj, h_eq]\n1609 | \n1610 | #print axioms prod_conj_partition_dual\n1611 | #print axioms plaquetteBoltzmannPD_inv\n1612 | #print axioms charProduct_PD\n1613 | #print axioms plaquette_product_separable_decomp\n1614 | \n1615 | /-- **Interface kernel character expansion (separable form).** Given a product of\n1616 | plaquette Boltzmann factors `∏_p exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃⁻¹g₄⁻¹))` over a finite set of\n1617 | interface plaquettes (with `c ≥ 0`), and a partition of the link set `L` into three\n1618 | disjoint Finsets `L_U` (positive-time \"U⁺\" links), `L_0` (interface \"u⁰\" links), and\n1619 | `L_V` (the \"V⁺\" links that appear conjugated after the reflection / change of\n1620 | variables), the product admits the *separable* character expansion\n1621 | \n1622 |     ∏_p exp(c·Re Tr(…)) = ∑_w F(w) · Φ_w(U⁺) · Ψ_w(u⁰) · conj(Φ_w(V⁺))\n1623 | \n1624 | with `F(w) ≥ 0`, where `Φ_w(U⁺) = ∏_{l ∈ L_U} χ_{w(l)}(g_l)`,\n1625 | `Ψ_w(u⁰) = ∏_{l ∈ L_0} χ_{w(l)}(g_l)`, and the V⁺ factor uses the dual\n1626 | (contragredient) map: `conj(Φ_w(V⁺)) = conj(∏_{l ∈ L_V} χ_{dual(w(l))}(g_l))`.\n1627 | \n1628 | This is the key input to the reflection-positivity argument (§8.1 of\n1629 | `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md`): the V⁺ links always appear with\n1630 | conjugated characters, so the kernel factors as a positive-coefficient sum of\n1631 | separated U⁺/u⁰/V⁺ character products. The proof composes\n1632 | `plaquette_product_separable_decomp` (which gives `∑_w F(w)·∏_l χ_{w(l)}(g_l)`)\n1633 | with `prod_conj_partition_dual` (which separates the V⁺ links with conjugated\n1634 | dual characters) and the disjoint union split `univ \\ L_V = L_U ∪ L_0`. -/\n1635 | lemma interface_kernel_character_expansion\n1636 |     {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {dims : ι → ℕ}\n1637 |     (ρ : ∀ i, SU N →* Matrix (Fin (dims i)) (Fin (dims i)) ℂ)\n1638 |     (hU : ∀ i, IsUnitaryRepresentation (ρ i))\n1639 |     (coeff : ι → ι → ι → ι → ι → ℝ) (hcoeff : ∀ r s t u v, 0 ≤ coeff r s t u v)\n1640 |     (cg : ι → ι → ι → ℝ) (hcg : ∀ s t w, 0 ≤ cg s t w)\n1641 |     (hcg_decomp : ∀ s t (g : SU N),\n1642 |       repCharacter (ρ s) g * repCharacter (ρ t) g =\n1643 |       ∑ w : ι, (cg s t w : ℂ) * repCharacter (ρ w) g)\n1644 |     (dual : ι → ι) (hdual : ∀ i (g : SU N),\n1645 |       repCharacter (ρ (dual i)) g = conj (repCharacter (ρ i) g))\n1646 |     (c : ℝ) (hc : 0 ≤ c)\n1647 |     (hexp4 : ∀ g₁ g₂ g₃ g₄ : SU N,\n1648 |       (Real.exp (c * (Matrix.trace ((g₁ * g₂ * g₃ * g₄ : SU N) :\n1649 |           Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ)).re) : ℂ) =\n1650 |         ∑ r : ι, ∑ s : ι, ∑ t : ι, ∑ u : ι, ∑ v : ι,\n1651 |           (coeff r s t u v : ℂ) *\n1652 |           (repCharacter (ρ s) g₁ * repCharacter (ρ t) g₂ *\n1653 |            repCharacter (ρ u) g₃ * repCharacter (ρ v) g₄))\n1654 |     (P : Type*) [Fintype P] [DecidableEq P]\n1655 |     (L : Type*) [Fintype L] [DecidableEq L]\n1656 |     (links : P → Fin 4 → L)\n1657 |     (hlinks_surj : ∀ l, ∃ p j, links p j = l)\n1658 |     (L_U L_0 L_V : Finset L)\n1659 |     (hdisj : Disjoint L_U L_0 ∧ Disjoint (L_U ∪ L_0) L_V)\n1660 |     (hcover : L_U ∪ L_0 ∪ L_V = Finset.univ) :\n1661 |     ∃ (F : (L → ι) → ℝ) (hF : ∀ w, 0 ≤ F w),\n1662 |       ∀ (g : L → SU N),\n1663 |       (∏ p : P, (Real.exp (c * (Matrix.trace\n1664 |           ((g (links p 0) * g (links