{"id":59,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean\n-- 1544 lines, 80022 bytes --\n420 | the TM kernel is Mercer-PD — which itself requires the Peter–Weyl character\n421 | expansion (approach (c) in the project docs).  See `Overview.lean` and\n422 | `README.md` for the full status. -/\n423 | \n424 | /-- A kernel `K : X → X → ℂ` is positive-definite (Mercer sense): for every\n425 | finite set `{x_i}` and coefficients `{c_i}`, the quadratic form\n426 | `∑ c_i * conj(c_j) * K(x_i, x_j) ≥ 0`. -/\n427 | def PositiveDefiniteKernel {X : Type*} (K : X → X → ℂ) : Prop :=\n428 |   ∀ (s : Finset X) (c : X → ℂ),\n429 |     0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * K i j\n430 | \n431 | /-- Helper: sum over fibers of a function.  For any `f : α → X`, the sum\n432 | `∑ i ∈ s, w i * Φ (f i)` can be regrouped by the value of `f i`. -/\n433 | private lemma sum_fiber_kernel {α X : Type*} [DecidableEq X]\n434 |     (s : Finset α) (f : α → X) (w : α → ℂ) (Φ : X → ℂ) :\n435 |     ∑ i ∈ s, w i * Φ (f i) =\n436 |     ∑ g ∈ s.image f, (∑ i ∈ s.filter (fun i => f i = g), w i) * Φ g := by\n437 |   let t := s.image f\n438 |   have hmaps : ∀ i ∈ s, f i ∈ t := fun i hi => Finset.mem_image_of_mem f hi\n439 |   rw [← Finset.sum_fiberwise_of_maps_to hmaps]\n440 |   refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun g hg => ?_)\n441 |   have hfg : ∀ i ∈ s.filter (fun i => f i = g), f i = g := fun i hi =>\n442 |     (Finset.mem_filter.mp hi).2\n443 |   have hsum : ∑ i ∈ s.filter (fun i => f i = g), w i * Φ (f i) =\n444 |       ∑ i ∈ s.filter (fun i => f i = g), w i * Φ g := by\n445 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n446 |     intro i hi; rw [hfg i hi]\n447 |   rw [hsum, ← Finset.sum_mul]\n448 | \n449 | /-- For a Mercer-PD kernel, the quadratic form with a mapped index set\n450 | is non-negative.  This is the key grouping argument: even if `f : α → X` is\n451 | not injective, the sum `∑ c_i conj(c_j) K(f i, f j)` is non-negative. -/\n452 | lemma PositiveDefiniteKernel.sum_nonneg_of_map\n453 |     {X : Type*} {K : X → X → ℂ} (hK : PositiveDefiniteKernel K)\n454 |     {α : Type*} (s : Finset α) (f : α → X) (c : α → ℂ) :\n455 |     0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * K (f i) (f j) := by\n456 |   classical\n457 |   let t := s.image f\n458 |   let d : X → ℂ := fun g => ∑ i ∈ s.filter (fun i => f i = g), c i\n459 |   have h_conj_d : ∀ h, ∑ j ∈ s.filter (fun j => f j = h), conj (c j) = conj (d h) := by\n460 |     intro h\n461 |     simp only [d, ← map_sum (starRingEnd ℂ)]\n462 |   have h_fiber_i : ∀ j ∈ s, ∑ i ∈ s, c i * K (f i) (f j) =\n463 |       ∑ g ∈ t, d g * K g (f j) := by\n464 |     intro j hj\n465 |     exact sum_fiber_kernel s f c (fun g => K g (f j))\n466 |   have h_fiber_j : ∀ g ∈ t, ∑ j ∈ s, conj (c j) * K g (f j) =\n467 |       ∑ h ∈ t, conj (d h) * K g h := by\n468 |     intro g hg\n469 |     rw [sum_fiber_kernel s f (fun j => conj (c j)) (fun h => K g h)]\n470 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n471 |     intro h hh\n472 |     rw [h_conj_d h]\n473 |   calc\n474 |     ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * K (f i) (f j)\n475 |         = ∑ j ∈ s, ∑ i ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * K (f i) (f j) := by\n476 |       rw [Finset.sum_comm]\n477 |     _ = ∑ j ∈ s, conj (c j) * ∑ i ∈ s, c i * K (f i) (f j) := by\n478 |       apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n479 |       intro j hj\n\n... 1065 more line(s) below (use offset=480 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-10 01:14:21 UTC","timestamp":1786324461,"token_count":1035,"tool_call_id":"41fcbc4b-544a-47e7-9d49-10b79832a4d6","full_token_estimate":823,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":1544,"byte_count":80022,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":43,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":60,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PeterWeyl.lean\n-- 3735 lines, 209363 bytes --\n555 | via the Clebsch-Gordan decomposition: `χ_s(g)·χ_t(g) = ∑_w cg s t w · χ_w(g)`\n556 | with `cg s t w ≥ 0`, and each `χ_w` is PD by `repCharacter_positiveDefinite`.\n557 | \n558 | (Note: PD-ness of the product also follows directly from the Schur product\n559 | theorem `PositiveDefinite.mul`.  This lemma additionally provides the explicit\n560 | non-negative character decomposition, which is the key ingredient for combining\n561 | character expansions across plaquettes that share a link variable.) -/\n562 | lemma charProduct_PD {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {dims : ι → ℕ}\n563 |     (ρ : ∀ i, SU N →* Matrix (Fin (dims i)) (Fin (dims i)) ℂ)\n564 |     (hU : ∀ i, IsUnitaryRepresentation (ρ i))\n565 |     (cg : ι → ι → ι → ℝ) (hcg : ∀ s t w, 0 ≤ cg s t w)\n566 |     (hcg_decomp : ∀ s t (g : SU N),\n567 |       repCharacter (ρ s) g * repCharacter (ρ t) g =\n568 |       ∑ w : ι, (cg s t w : ℂ) * repCharacter (ρ w) g)\n569 |     (s t : ι) :\n570 |     PositiveDefinite (fun g => repCharacter (ρ s) g * repCharacter (ρ t) g) := by\n571 |   simp only [hcg_decomp s t]\n572 |   exact PositiveDefinite.sum Finset.univ (fun w => repCharacter (ρ w))\n573 |     (fun w _ => repCharacter_SU_positiveDefinite ρ hU w) (cg s t)\n574 |     (fun w _ => hcg s t w)\n575 | \n576 | /-- A finite product of characters of the same group element decomposes as a\n577 | non-negative-weighted sum of single characters, via iterated Clebsch-Gordan.\n578 | \n579 | For a nonempty finite set `s` of representation indices, `∏_{i ∈ s} χ_i(g)`\n580 | can be written as `∑_w coeff w · χ_w(g)` with `coeff w ≥ 0`.  This is proved by\n581 | induction on `s`, applying the CG decomposition `χ_s·χ_t = ∑_w cg s t w · χ_w`\n582 | at each step.  The coefficient of `χ_v` in the product over `insert x s` is\n583 | `∑_w coeff_s(w) · cg x w v`, which is non-negative as a sum of products of\n584 | non-negative reals.\n585 | \n586 | This is the key algebraic ingredient for the transfer-matrix kernel\n587 | decomposition: when a single link variable appears in multiple interface\n588 | plaquettes, the product of the character expansions produces a product of\n589 | characters of that link, which this lemma reduces to a single non-negative\n590 | sum. -/\n591 | lemma charProduct_finset_decomp {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {dims : ι → ℕ}\n592 |     (ρ : ∀ i, SU N →* Matrix (Fin (dims i)) (Fin (dims i)) ℂ)\n593 |     (hU : ∀ i, IsUnitaryRepresentation (ρ i))\n594 |     (cg : ι → ι → ι → ℝ) (hcg : ∀ s t w, 0 ≤ cg s t w)\n595 |     (hcg_decomp : ∀ s t (g : SU N),\n596 |       repCharacter (ρ s) g * repCharacter (ρ t) g =\n597 |       ∑ w : ι, (cg s t w : ℂ) * repCharacter (ρ w) g)\n598 |     (s : Finset ι) (hs : s.Nonempty) :\n599 |     ∃ (coeff : ι → ℝ) (hcoeff : ∀ w, 0 ≤ coeff w),\n600 |       ∀ (g : SU N),\n601 |         (∏ i ∈ s, repCharacter (ρ i) g) =\n602 |         ∑ w : ι, (coeff w : ℂ) * repCharacter (ρ w) g := by\n603 |   classical\n604 |   induction s using Finset.induction_on with\n605 |   | empty => exact (Finset.not_nonempty_empty hs).elim\n606 |   | insert x s hx ih =>\n607 |     by_cases hse : s = ∅\n608 |     · -- Singleton: ∏_{i ∈ {x}} χ_i(g) = χ_x(g) = 1 · χ_x(g)\n609 |       subst hse\n610 |       refine ⟨fun w => if w = x then 1 else 0, fun w => ?_, fun g => ?_⟩\n611 |       · show 0 ≤ (if w = x then 1 else 0)\n612 |         split_ifs <;> norm_num\n613 |       · -- ∏ i ∈ {x}, χ_i(g) = χ_x(g) = ∑ w, (if w = x then 1 else 0) * χ_w(g)\n614 |         rw [Finset.prod_insert hx, Finset.prod_empty, mul_one]\n\n... 3121 more line(s) below (use offset=615 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-10 01:14:21 UTC","timestamp":1786324461,"token_count":1132,"tool_call_id":"77271f14-6b8c-4ed6-940d-b81126733dd7","full_token_estimate":809,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PeterWeyl.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_c