{"id":65,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean\n-- 1544 lines, 80022 bytes --\n 95 | functions with non-negative weights is PD).  The proof swaps the finite PD\n 96 | quadratic-form sum with the integral (justified by the integrability\n 97 | hypothesis) and uses that the integrand is non-negative `ν`-a.e. by the\n 98 | positive-definiteness of each `Φ t`. -/\n 99 | lemma PositiveDefinite.integral {T : Type*} [MeasurableSpace T] (ν : Measure T)\n100 |     (Φ : T → G → ℂ) (hPD : ∀ᵐ t ∂ν, PositiveDefinite (Φ t))\n101 |     (hint : ∀ g : G, Integrable (fun t => Φ t g) ν) :\n102 |     PositiveDefinite (fun g => ∫ t, Φ t g ∂ν) := by\n103 |   intro s c\n104 |   -- The PD quadratic-form integrand is non-negative ν-a.e.\n105 |   have h_nonneg : ∀ᵐ t ∂ν,\n106 |       0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) := by\n107 |     filter_upwards [hPD] with t hPDt\n108 |     exact hPDt s c\n109 |   -- Integrability of each (i,j) summand, in `*` form.\n110 |   have h_int_ij : ∀ i ∈ s, ∀ j ∈ s, Integrable\n111 |       (fun t => c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) ν := by\n112 |     intro i _ j _\n113 |     have h := (hint (i⁻¹ * j)).smul (c i * conj (c j))\n114 |     rwa [show (c i * conj (c j)) • (fun t => Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) =\n115 |         (fun t => c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) from by\n116 |         funext t; rw [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]] at h\n117 |   have h_int_i : ∀ i ∈ s, Integrable\n118 |       (fun t => ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) ν :=\n119 |     fun i hi => integrable_finsetSum s (h_int_ij i hi)\n120 |   -- Swap the finite sum and the integral.\n121 |   have h_swap :\n122 |       (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * ∫ t, Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) ∂ν) =\n123 |       ∫ t, ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) ∂ν := by\n124 |     symm\n125 |     rw [integral_finsetSum s h_int_i]\n126 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n127 |     intro i hi\n128 |     rw [integral_finsetSum s (h_int_ij i hi)]\n129 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n130 |     intro j _\n131 |     rw [show (fun t => c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) =\n132 |         (fun t => (c i * conj (c j)) • Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) from by\n133 |         funext t; rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc]]\n134 |     rw [integral_smul, smul_eq_mul]\n135 |   -- Beta-reduce the goal to match h_swap, then conclude.\n136 |   have h_beta :\n137 |       (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * (fun g => ∫ t, Φ t g ∂ν) (i⁻¹ * j)) =\n138 |       (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * ∫ t, Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) ∂ν) := by\n139 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n140 |     intro i _\n141 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n142 |     intro j _\n143 |     rfl\n144 |   rw [h_beta, h_swap]\n145 |   -- The integral is non-negative: split into real and imaginary parts.\n146 |   have h_re_nonneg : ∀ᵐ t ∂ν,\n147 |       0 ≤ (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)).re := by\n148 |     filter_upwards [h_nonneg] with t ht\n149 |     exact (Complex.nonneg_iff.mp ht).1\n150 |   have h_im_zero : ∀ᵐ t ∂ν,\n151 |       (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)).im = 0 := by\n152 |     filter_upwards [h_nonneg] with t ht\n153 |     exact (Complex.nonneg_iff.mp ht).2.symm\n154 |   have h_int' : Integrable\n155 |       (fun t => ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) ν := by\n156 |     have heq : (fun t => ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)) =\n157 |         fun t => ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, (c i * conj (c j)) • Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) := by\n158 |       funext t; simp only [smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc]\n159 |     rw [heq]\n160 |     exact integrable_finsetSum s (fun i hi => integrable_finsetSum s (h_int_ij i hi))\n161 |   have h_im_zero' : (fun t => (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)).im) =ᵐ[ν] 0 :=\n162 |     h_im_zero\n163 |   have h_int_re : (∫ t, ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) ∂ν).re =\n164 |       ∫ t, (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)).re ∂ν :=\n165 |     (integral_re h_int').symm\n166 |   have h_int_im : (∫ t, ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j) ∂ν).im =\n167 |       ∫ t, (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * Φ t (i⁻¹ * j)).im ∂ν :=\n168 |     (integral_im h_int').symm\n169 |   rw [ge_iff_le, Complex.nonneg_iff]\n170 |   refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩\n171 |   · rw [h_int_re]\n172 |     exact integral_nonneg_of_ae h_re_nonneg\n173 |   · rw [h_int_im]\n174 |     rw [integral_eq_zero_of_ae h_im_zero']\n175 | \n176 | /-! ## Positive integral operators from positive-definite kernels\n177 | \n178 | The main result here is `PositiveDefinite.integralOperator_nonneg`: for a\n179 | compact (pseudo)metric group `G` with probability measure `μ`, a continuous\n180 | positive-definite function `φ`, and a continuous function `f`, the integral\n181 | `∫∫ f(x) * conj(f(y)) * φ(x⁻¹ * y) dμ dμ ≥ 0`.\n182 | \n183 | This is the continuous analogue of the definition of positive-definiteness\n184 | itself: the quadratic form `∑ c_i * conj(c_j) * φ(g_i⁻¹ * g_j) ≥ 0` becomes\n185 | an integral in the limit.  The proof approximates the integral by Riemann\n186 | sums; each Riemann sum is non-negative by `PositiveDefinite.sum_nonneg_of_map`,\n187 | and the sums converge to the integral by uniform continuity of the integrand\n188 | on the compact space `G × G`.\n189 | \n190 | No Haar-measure invariance is needed: the non-negativity of each Riemann sum\n191 | is a direct consequence of the positive-definiteness of `φ`. -/\n192 | \n193 | lemma PositiveDefinite.integralOperator_nonneg\n194 |     {G : Type*} [Group G] [PseudoMetricSpace G] [CompactSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]\n\n... 1350 more line(s) below (use offset=195 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-10 01:18:15 UTC","timestamp":1786324695,"token_count":1734,"tool_call_id":"b90d8dce-dd7b-4387-b8d6-0b710a1e36f5","full_token_estimate":1271,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line