{"id":98,"role":"Assistant","content":"","timestamp":1786326889,"token_count":0,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"action\":\"update\",\"task_items\":[{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-06 through 2026-08-09 sessions 38-72): Lüscher roadmap, character expansion, cascade lemmas, topology analysis, gauge invariance investigation, §8.11.53-59 analysis. See completed items 90-122 for details.\",\"id\":\"90\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-10 session 73): CRITICAL ANALYSIS (§8.11.60). The §8.11.59 'PD for each u⁰' claim is WRONG. The interface kernel K_{u⁰}(U⁺, W⁺) = exp(-β S_int(U⁺, u⁰, θW⁺)) is NOT a PD kernel for each fixed u⁰ because the character expansion coefficients Ψ_w(u⁰) = ∏ χ_{w(l)}(g_l) are COMPLEX-valued (not non-negative reals). The §8.11.58 obstruction (matrix J_l NOT PSD on spatial interface links) SURVIVES the change of variables — the change of variables resolves the S_pos/S_neg asymmetry but does NOT resolve the spatial interface link issue. The full integral reduces to I = Σ_w F(w)·∫ Ψ_w(u⁰)·|A_w(u⁰)|² dμ⁰, which is EXACTLY the §8.11.58 structure. Build GREEN, 0 sorries, 6 axioms. No code changes — analysis + §8.11.60 documentation only.\",\"id\":\"123\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"PENDING — NEW DIRECTION (§8.11.60): The correct proof mechanism for transferMatrixPositivity_axiom is UNKNOWN. The §8.11.59 approach (change of variables + 'PD for each u⁰') does NOT work. The §8.11.58 obstruction is REAL. Three options to investigate: (a) The bulk Boltzmann factor exp(-β S_pos) compensates for negative spatial interface terms — requires showing the FULL sum Σ_w F(w)·∫ Ψ_w·|A_w|² ≥ 0 (not individual terms). The §8.11.58 U(1) counterexample was WITHOUT the bulk Boltzmann factor; the full integral may still be non-negative. (b) Re-introduce gauge invariance (IsGaugeInvariant N f) — the Lüscher mechanism constrains spatial interface link dependence. (c) Strengthen the support hypothesis to dependsOnlyOnPositive (f depends only on U⁺, NOT on any interface links) — then u⁰ integral kills all non-trivial characters by orthogonality, giving non-negativity. NOTE: The Osterwalder-Seiler theorem IS true (the integral IS non-negative), but the mechanism is NOT 'PD for each u⁰'. The change of variables (step A) is fully formalized and correct. The character expansion (step 2) and temporal collapse (step 4) are formalized. What's missing is the correct mechanism for the spatial interface links. Key existing infra: transferMatrix_change_of_variables (TransferMatrix.lean:2619), transferMatrix_integral_reduction (TransferMatrix.lean:5160), osG_thetaG_eq_char_expansion_pointwise (ReflectionPositivity.lean:2818), integral_prod_repCharacter_trivial (PeterWeyl.lean), interface_kernel_character_expansion (PeterWeyl.lean:1635), plaquetteBoltzmannPD (PeterWeyl.lean:367), PositiveDefiniteKernel.integralOperator_nonneg (PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:553).\",\"id\":\"48\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}","name":"project_task_list"},"id":"12113681-7ba3-49c4-ada7-38fa5e5f1d9c","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":734,"reasoning_content":"I'm at 64% context. I've completed my analysis and documented it. Let me update the project task list with the new finding and then decide whether to continue investigating or hand off.\n\nThe key finding is that the §8.11.59 \"PD for each u⁰\" claim is wrong. This is a significant discovery that changes the direction. I should update the project task list to reflect this and then hand off, since the next step requires deep investigation into the correct mechanism (which is a new research direction).\n\nLet me update the project task list.","turn":77,"is_prune_marker":false}
